From adb243fb9a1a06ccb1f9126f264e098bad92378e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Horizon authors <>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 22:21:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Patch 0183: LANGUAGE and MAP SIGNS in OPTIONS: the game in
 English or Spanish, switched at run time
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The executable is built twice from one tree (LANG_BUILD=en/es): gen_text.py pads every string to the longer of its two
texts and shares an array only when both languages agree (TEXT_BANK_PAD), the literals become arrays, and the numbers that
depend on the language (the rects of the Spanish words drawn in the textures, the packed rows' crops and pieces, the
BATTLE banner's blocks, the ○PULSA and Press Start quads) are data tables chosen with MOD_LANG_BUILD around their
values only; tools/langpatch.py checks that the two builds differ in no function and writes the other language's
bytes (LANGEN.BIN / LANGES.BIN), which modSetLanguage copies over the strings at the title, then reads the script text
again and uploads FI_INFO.TIM again. modLangFile (lookupFileTable) reads a file's Spanish copy, and a map background's
copy with the signs translated unless MAP SIGNS is ORIGINAL, from LANG_FILES (the Makefile: name, Spanish copy, copy
with English signs). OPTIONS: two rows more (LANGUAGE ENGLISH/ESPAÑOL, MAP SIGNS ORIGINAL/TRANSLATED), the values two
rows share drawn once in the text area; saved in SAVE_TAG_OPTIONS bytes 7 and 8. Also: the battle end box draws the
mod font's two-byte glyphs (accents were blank); the slot menus draw the slot-2 rows whole (a 2 drawn at the US
text's x landed wrong with font b and in Spanish); the feed menu's and the evolution chart's strings keyed
(text/main/mod_feed.yaml, CHART_STR_*); the C files' .rodata of plain sections kept by the link scripts
(docs/mods/language.md)
